  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23516135.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Broad-scale Zooplankton Surveys in 1994-1998",
  "description": "Fish eggs and larvae and zooplankton were sampled along 15-20 transect lines off the southern Washington and Oregon coasts, from 2 to 100 miles from shore during July 1994 and 1995, June 1996, and July 1997 and 1998. Plankton sampling was done with a 25 cm CalVET net fitted with 150 µm mesh nets. CTD casts to 70 m were done and nutrient and chlorophyll samples were collected from 3 m depth at each station. [ Reference: PICES Scientific Report No. 18 2001, Proceedings of the PICES/CoML/IPRC Workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\", http://www.pices.int/publications/scientific_reports/Report18/default.aspx. ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To map the distribution and abundance of anchovy and sardines eggs and larvae in relation to hydrography and zooplankton abundance.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23516136",
